WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.680
Traditionally biomedical research, when you
do an experiment, it tries to reduce the heterogeneity

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:13.790
in the data to make sure that when the conclusions
are made there is no known confounding factor.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:18.280
What we have been focusing on is using a lot
of data that's very heterogeneous —

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:25.600
some might call it dirty data — and use this
large amount of dirty data to identify a signal

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.660
for a disease that is conserved across multiple
independent data sets and is clinically useful.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:37.000
And we've shown that this approach works in
a broad number of data sets, a broad number

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.810
of diseases — including autoimmune diseases,
organ transplants, infectious diseases, cancers

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:49.060
— for identifying diagnostic and prognostic
markers, new drug targets, and so on.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:58.179
We applied our dirty data approach to identify
a diagnostic signature for tuberculosis.

00:00:58.179 --> 00:01:04.740
One third of the world is infected with latent
tuberculosis and about 180, 190 million people

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.800
worldwide have active disease.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.380
But even in the 21st Century it's very difficult
to diagnose active TB.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:20.810
And what we were able to show is that using
almost 2,600 blood samples from 11 different

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:26.380
countries in 14 independent cohorts, we found
that there is a three-gene signature that

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:33.561
distinguishes who has active TB from who has
latent TB, who has other diseases that look

00:01:33.561 --> 00:01:38.299
like TB, and who are completely healthy with
a very high accuracy.

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:43.539
Now what we are working on showing is that
it also allows us to predict who's going to

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:47.430
have active TB much, much earlier than clinical
diagnosis.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:55.600
It collates with treatment response and that
it can be used as a screening tool for identifying

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.260
the patients who may have active TB and should
be treated as soon as possible

